@page
@model PTPBank.Web.Pages.AboutModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
}

<nav aria-label="breadcrumb" class="breadcrumb-wrap">
    <ol class="breadcrumb">
        <li class="breadcrumb-item"><a asp-page="/Index">Home</a></li>
        <li class="breadcrumb-item active" aria-current="page">About</li>
    </ol>
</nav>

<div class="surface-panel">
    <h1 class="page-title">About PTPBank</h1>
    <p>PTPBank is a comprehensive banking management system designed to streamline core retail banking workflows in a clean, maintainable architecture.</p>

    <h2 class="section-heading mt-4 mb-3">What PTPBank Delivers</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Centralized <strong>Person</strong> records with robust input validation.</li>
        <li>Structured <strong>Account</strong> management for Savings and Cheque products.</li>
        <li>Reliable <strong>Transaction</strong> processing with integrity checks and audit-friendly flows.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="section-heading mt-4 mb-3">Technology Stack</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>.NET Core 8 and Razor Pages</li>
        <li>Entity Framework Core</li>
        <li>SQL Server</li>
        <li>Bootstrap 5 + jQuery UI</li>
        <li>FluentValidation</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="section-heading mt-4 mb-3">Architecture &amp; Patterns</h2>
    <p class="mb-0">The solution follows layered architecture principles with Repository, Unit of Work, Service Layer, DTO, and Factory patterns. This keeps business rules centralized, preserves data integrity, and supports long-term maintainability.</p>
</div>
